      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\n\n\nAdd `spaces_between_special_tokens` to `ResponsesRequest` so Kimi K3's `adjust_request` can turn it off on responses API endpoint, as it already does on chat completions API. Without it, XTML markers leak into Responses API output text.\n\nSupersedes #51152, which has had merge conflicts since 2026-09-02 and no response from its author despite follow-ups. Original author credited via `Co-authored-by`.\n\n## Claims\n\n\n\n- `ResponsesRequest` accepts `spaces_between_special_tokens` (default `True`, same as `ChatCompletionRequest`) and passes it to `SamplingParams`. Requests that don't set it behave as before.\n\n## Validation\n\n\n\n### Minimal reproducer of the bug\n\n```python\nfrom openai import OpenAI\n\nclient = OpenAI(base_url=\"http://localhost:8080/v1\", api_key=\"DUMMY\")\nmessages = [\n    {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What time is it now in New York?\"},\n    {\n        \"type\": \"function_call\",\n        \"call_id\": \"chatcmpl-tool-9a1b108b61cbb7cf\",\n        \"name\": \"getCurrentTime\",\n        \"arguments\": \"{\\\"location\\\": \\\"New York\\\"}\",\n    },\n    {\n        \"type\": \"function_call_output\",\n        \"call_id\": \"chatcmpl-tool-9a1b108b61cbb7cf\",\n        \"output\": \" Current time in New York is 2026-10-14 00:05:21.\",\n    },\n]\nfor e in client.responses.create(model=\"moonshotai/Kimi-K3\", input=messages, stream=True):\n    t = getattr(e, \"type\", \"\")\n    if t in (\"response.output_text.delta\", \"response.refusal.delta\"):\n        print(e.delta.content or \"\", end=\"\")\n```\n\n| | Streamed output text |\n|---|---|\n| `main` | `<\\|open\\|> response Current time in New York is ...` |\n| this PR | `Current time in New York is ...` |\n\n### Updated unit tests\n\n```bash\npytest tests/reasoning/test_kimi_k3_reasoning_parser.py -v\npytest tests/tool_use/test_kimi_k3_tool_parser.py -v\n```\n\n```log\n...\n=================================================================================================== 52 passed in 0.25s ====================================================================================================\n\n...\n=================================================================================================== 27 passed in 9.04s ====================================================================================================\n```\n\n## Details\n\n\n\n#51152 also reports trailing/leading spaces in string tool-call arguments on `/v1/responses` (e.g. `\" Tokyo \"`). That symptom has the same cause, so this change fixes it too.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
